\mutenow mutes one or more instruments immediately.
Its syntax is the following:

\mutenow \violin \cello

where \violin and \cello are instruments created with
\insts.init. To mute all instruments, call:

\mutenow \all

Unlike \mute, which waits for the start of the next bar,
\mutenow mutes the instruments at once, even in the middle
of a bar.
To bring them back, use \unmutenow or \unmute.

A muted instrument shows a whole rest in the score and is
hidden in the piano roll.

\mutenow needs at least one argument, and an argument that
is not an instrument results in an "unknown instrument"
error.
